{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1184852-how-does-forging-weapons-work","id":1184852,"title":"How does forging weapons work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-11T13:03:43-08:00","id":1184852,"title":"How does forging weapons work?","content":"Hi there, i'm pretty new here and I've been playing on Samp a server that is dedicated to WoDish gameplay and I'm here to ask a question relating weapon forging/Crafting/smithing.I'm a gargoyle and I'm hoping to know how does rolling work for weapon crafting, what skills and attributes are used and what knowledge would I need to do some simple blacksmithing or some more advanced metalurgy even.I'm not sure where I could ask this question so I'm sorry if I missed the section entirelly it's my first time here.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for difficulties for most weapons, like polarms, swords, two handed and shield related weaponry, so I'd like to roleplay something of a support character to some of my allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T14:23:10-08:00","id":1184891,"title":"","content":"The books, for the most part, don't go into a lot of detail on this.<br /> <br /> The Crafts Skill is obviously relevant to any rolls. Intelligence (or Wits for jury-rigging/etc.) is generally used for designing something. Dexterity would be the default for physically crafting something, though Strength and Stamina might be brought in by some STs (forging battle worthy blades even with modern power tools requires a good deal of strength and endurance).<br /> <br /> A vampire specifically might have to make a Virtue check when dealing with flames/extreme heat because of the risk of harming themselves and all that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T09:37:28-08:00","id":1185979,"title":"","content":"I'll asume you've got a gargoyle power to help deal with the terror of flames for making steel.<br /> <br /> You could do an extended roll with crafts and I believe a mental stat. Forging isn't a one night process. A lot of stuff'll take months.<br /> strength and stamina are obviously important for blacksmiths, but the ability to bang on things for a long duration isn't going to dictate the quality of the work. I'd say perception (judging the right temperatures, getting everything level, spotting imperfections and such) is the attribute you'll most use.<br /> <br /> Another important thing is that some items use different skill sets or you'd use different people. Shields are sometimes all metal, but most often they're mostly wood, polarms and archery only give the relevant amount of work to the blacksmith. <br /> <br /> There's a scale somewhere between nails for carpentry and full plate,but honestly whilst some things are just outright hard to do, some stuff's just laborious. A full suit of mail isn't hard, it's just a lot of work. <br /> <br /> Lastly, unless you're a masterwork artist the likes of which the toreador'd take, there's not really much point in a vampire becoming a smith. Just use money, get a ghoul, or since you're a gargoyle who probably knows a couple of thaumaturges, there's the path of conjuring. It's a strange unlife choice you're making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":23728,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","user":"PewPew","date":". 02-14-2018, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T10:11:19-08:00","id":1187591,"title":"","content":"Based on what I've read it seems that Perception + Crafts is generally used for creation rolls with difficulty and number of required successes varying based on the task in question. Smithing would fall under the Armorsmithing or Blacksmithing Fields of Expertise for Crafts. There are powers which can benefit the crafting of one's own arms (see Breakdown below).<ul><li>If an ST wanted to incentive crafting one's own weapons or have a benefit to seeking master smiths I can envision a number of ways to do that.<ul><li>Master crafts might be offered as recompense or gifts to others</li> <li>Some small bonus to using the weapon (I would avoid direct increased damage dice since that is covered by Potence powers below) or wearing the armor, I offer the following suggestions<ul><li>For Weapons<ul><li>Decrease on the required Minimum Strength to use. A master smith can use forging and fullers to reduce the weight of a weapon without sacrificing power.</li> <li>Offer a bonus to use certain combat maneuvers. A sword with an improved guard might offer a +1 bonus on a parry, while another with an enhanced blade might offer a +1 bonus on sweeping as just a pair of examples</li> <li>Increase the Range of Ranged Weapons by some measure.</li> </ul></li> <li>For Armor<ul><li>Increasing the threshold for damage required to break the armor (which normally occurs when an attack's damage roll does twice the armor's rating)</li> <li>Reduce the Dexterity penalty for wearing the armor</li> <li>Offer a bonus against certain maneuvers like special gauntlet might offer a bonus against disarm (counting as an extra dot of strength for the purposes of successes required to disarm) or thicker armor might offer a +1 bonus on a tackle</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> Breakdown of what info I found:<ul><li>Vampire the Dark Ages 20th Anniversary (DAV20) has the following regarding Crafting:<ul><li>The Crafts skill has a number of fields of expertise suggested. Those important to forging would be Armorsmithing and Blacksmithing<ul><li>I'm assuming if they had intended Weaponsmithing to be a separate field it would have been listed since they listed Armorsmithing</li> </ul></li> <li>Crafting is described as being variable with Perception + Craft being a common roll.</li> <li>The Auspex 1 Celerity 1 Combination Power The Master Artisan that allows the Cainite to use their enhanced speed and perception to speed creation<ul><li>Spend 1 BP - Craft in a minute what would take an hour</li> <li>With multiple blood points, she can create enormous art installations or even houses in under an hour.</li> <li>Spend 1 blood point to create what would take a minute in a three-second turn.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Dark Ages: Vampire, the edition previous to DAV20:<ul><li>Perception + Crafts for creation and maintenance as well, though it offers that maintaining a weapon can be done with the appropriate combat ability (Archery or Melee) at difficulty 6.</li> <li>Guide to the High Clans has Intelligence + Crafts as the roll for forging a weapon under the Potence 6 Power Master of the Forge which the Cainite can use to grant the weapon incredible durability to withstand the stress of high strength users and increased damage by one.</li> </ul></li> <li>Vampire: The Dark Ages, the edition previous to Dark Ages: Vampire:<ul><li>Dark Ages: Companion has the Potence Level 7 Power The Forger's Hammer which allows the Cainite to make a Strength + Crafts roll to imbue the weapon with their immense strength, increasing the damage by one for every two successes and inflicting Aggravated wounds.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}